---
import PageFrame from './PageFrame.astro';
import PageMasthead from './PageMasthead.astro';
---
<main>
  <PageFrame as="section">
    <h1>Page frames</h1>
    <p><a href="/catalogue/">All components</a> · <a href="/systems/">Systems</a> · <a href="/foundations/">Foundations</a> · <a href="/about/">About</a></p>
    <p>The same centred frame supplies page width, gutters and opening space. Resize the browser to compare the examples.</p>
  </PageFrame>
  <PageFrame inset="none" opening="none" ending="none">
    <PageMasthead label="Page-title band" />
  </PageFrame>
  <PageFrame as="article" class="reading-example">
    <h2>Reading page</h2>
    <p>A bounded text column sits inside the shared page frame. Its line length stays readable while the outer frame aligns with directories and navigation.</p>
  </PageFrame>
  <PageFrame as="section" opening="none" ending="large">
    <header class="directory-opening"><h2>Directory page</h2><p>A directory can arrange its opening and entries freely inside the same gutters.</p></header>
    <div class="directory-entries"><a href="/systems/">Explore machines</a><a href="/foundations/">Explore shared ideas</a></div>
  </PageFrame>
  <PageFrame as="section" class="full-example">
    <h2>The same outer frame</h2>
    <p>Every section uses the same outer width and responsive gutter. Inner content can use a narrower reading measure.</p>
  </PageFrame>
</main>
<style>
  h1, h2 { margin: 0 0 24px; }
  p { max-width: 65ch; margin: 16px 0; }
  .reading-example, .full-example { border-block: 1px solid var(--h-line); }
  .directory-opening { padding-block: 40px 48px; }
  .directory-entries { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 24px; }
  .directory-entries a { padding-block: 24px; border-top: 1px solid var(--h-line); }
  @media(max-width:600px) { .directory-entries { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
